# Code owners decide who can approve a pull request. The main-branch ruleset requires an
# approving review from a code owner for every file a pull request changes.
#
# Roles (see GOVERNANCE.md):
#   owner            @madkatomega-sys
#   pr-approver      may approve code, docs, and config changes
#   contrib-approver may approve additions to the approved-contributors list
#
# To add someone to a role: invite them as a collaborator with the "Write" role (code owners
# must have write access), then add their @username to the matching lines below in a pull
# request. Changes to this file always need the owner's approval.
#
# The last matching pattern wins, so the general rule comes first.

# Everything: the owner or a pr-approver.
# pr-approvers: add usernames after the owner on this line.
*                                       @madkatomega-sys

# Governance, licensing, CI, and repository rules: the owner only.
